.TH README 1 2026\-10\-07 atexit TheCRatTime
.SH atexit
\fBatexit\fR \- forget about the forgotten \fBfree\fR(3)
.PP
.SH Description
This is a small project to prevent double free and
memory leak.\&
.PP
.SS Features
\fB\-\fR C89/ANSI C code standard.\&
.br
\fB\-\fR Minimal memory usage.\&
.br
\fB\-\fR Auto-free functions
.br
\fB\-\fR Auto-generation wrappers
.PP
.SS Quick start
.nf
.RS 4
#define ATEXIT_SOURCE
#include "atexit.\&h"

#define MAIN_VOID
#include "main_wrapper.\&h"

int Main(AtExitHeader* main_atexit) {
  char* buffer = AtExitMalloc(main_atexit, 4096);
  if (!buffer) {
    return 1;
  }

  /* do something.\&.\&.\& */

  /* No need write free() */
  return 0;
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SS Needed
\fB\-\fR C Compiler with support C89 standard.\&
.br
\fB\-\fR CMake 3.\&10 and greater
.PP
.SS Building
.nf
.RS 4
cmake -B build
cd build/
make
.fi
.RE
.PP
CMake have options:
.PP
\fBBUILD_EX\fR
.RS 4
Build examples in \fBexamples/\fR directory.\&
.br
Default: ON
.RE
.PP
\fBUSE_TESTS\fR
.RS 4
Build tests.\&
.br
Default: ON
.RE
.PP
.SS How add to your project
To use atexit in your project, you just move \fBinclude/*\fR to project:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
mkdir -p myproject/
cp -r include/ myproject/
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH Examples
You can find examples in \fBexamples/\fR directory.\&
